\begin{align*}9!\equiv & \frac{10!}{10}\\ \equiv & \frac{-1}{10}\\ \equiv & \frac{-1}{-1}\\ \equiv & 1\,\,({\bmod }11).\end{align*}
So the remainder is $1$.</think> <answer> $1$</answer>

